#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198004 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e74c46c7-7f57-5adc-8acb-ea91958d8725" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Taylor Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "6c5e3d93-e244-52da-845b-365bb94bd19d" :question/math-academy-id "e-12562" :question/problem "Determine the quadratic Taylor polynomial for the function of two variables\n$f(x,y) = \\cos(x+y)$\nabout the point $(0,0)$." :question/worked-solution "If the function $f(x,y)$ is twice differentiable at\n\n$$\n(x,y) = (0,0)\n$$\n\nthen the quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x, y) \\mid \\approx f(0, 0) + f_{x}(0, 0) \\cdot x + f_{y}(0, 0) \\cdot y^(⏞)^(Linear approximation); \\approx + \\frac{1}{2}(f_{xx}(0, 0) \\cdot x^{2} + 2f_{xy}(0, 0) \\cdot xy + f_{yy}(0, 0) \\cdot y^{2})_(⏟)_(Quadratic part)\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the terms of our Taylor polynomial.\n\n- Calculating the value of the function, we have\n$f(0, 0)|= 1$.\n- Calculating the first derivatives, we have the following:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}f_{x}(x, y)|=-\\sin (x + y), & f_{y}(x, y)|=-\\sin (x + y) \\\\ f_{x}(0, 0)|= 0, & f_{y}(0, 0)|= 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n- Calculating the second derivatives, we have the following:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}f_{xx}(x, y)|=-\\cos (x + y), & f_{xx}(0, 0)|=-1 \\\\ f_{xy}(x, y)|=-\\cos (x + y), & f_{xy}(0, 0)|=-1 \\\\ f_{yy}(x, y)|=-\\cos (x + y), & f_{yy}(0, 0)|=-1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nTherefore, the second-degree Taylor polynomial is given by\n\n$$\nf(x, y) \\mid \\approx 1 + 0 \\cdot x + 0 \\cdot y + \\frac{1}{2}((-1) \\cdot x^{2} + 2(-1) \\cdot xy + (-1) \\cdot y^{2}); = 1 - \\frac{1}{2}x^{2} - xy - \\frac{1}{2}y^{2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198005 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b91ae708-a63d-51ac-9ae0-f24724392858" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Taylor Polynomial in Matrix Form"}] :question/id #uuid "1d13a6c0-0912-5089-81ed-c298bf747ccd" :question/math-academy-id "e-12563" :question/problem "For the function $f:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R$, defined as\n\n$f\\left(x,y \\right) = x^2y-xy^3$,\n\ndetermine the quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ Give your answer in matrix form." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that the function $\\mathbf{f}:\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ x_{n}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nand is twice differentiable at\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = \\mathbf a\n$$\n\nThen, the quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $\\mathbf a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x) \\mid \\approx f(a) + f^{′}(a)(x - a) + \\frac{1}{2}(x - a)^{T}f^{″}(a)(x - a)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂x_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂x_{n}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}∂x_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}∂x_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}∂x_{1}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}∂x_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}∂x_{1}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}∂x_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix}, \\mid f^{″}(x)|= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x^{2}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂y^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the terms of our Taylor polynomial:\n\n- Calculating the value of the function, we have\n$f(1, 1)|= 0$.\n- Calculating the first derivatives, we have the following:\n$f^{′}(x)|= \\begin{bmatrix}2xy - y^{3} & x^{2} - 3xy^{2}\\end{bmatrix}; f^{′}(1, 1)|= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\n- Calculating the second derivative, we have the following:\n$f^{″}(x)|= \\begin{bmatrix}2y & 2x - 3y^{2} \\\\ 2x - 3y^{2} & -6xy\\end{bmatrix}; f^{″}(1, 1)|= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nTherefore, the second-degree Taylor polynomial (in matrix form) is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198006 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b19cc766-bdc5-5ab2-aa4d-ebddf8311116" :knowledge-point/title "Approximating a Multivariable Function at a Point Using a Quadratic Taylor Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "137d7caf-b232-5e21-9583-14d907a98624" :question/math-academy-id "e-12564" :question/problem "For the twice-differentiable function $f:\\mathbb R^3\\to\\mathbb R$, we have the following data:\n\n$f(1, 0, 0)|=-1, \\mid f^{′}(1, 0, 0)|= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, \\mid f^{″}(1, 0, 0)|= \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nUse the quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ to approximate the value of $f(1,1,1)$." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that the function $\\mathbf{f}:\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ x_{n}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nand is twice differentiable at\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = \\mathbf a\n$$\n\nThen, the quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $\\mathbf a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x) \\mid \\approx f(a) + f^{′}(a)(x - a) + \\frac{1}{2}(x - a)^{T}f^{″}(a)(x - a)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂x_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂x_{n}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}∂x_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}∂x_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}∂x_{1}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}∂x_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}∂x_{1}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}∂x_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and the following data:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(a) &= -1, \\mid f^{′}(a)|= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, \\mid f^{″}(a)|= \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second-degree Taylor polynomial is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the polynomial at $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf(1, 1, 1) \\mid \\approx - 1 + \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 - 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 - 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 - 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}; =-1 + \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}; =-1 + 1 + \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}; = \\frac{1}{2}(3); = \\frac{3}{2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198570 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b91ae708-a63d-51ac-9ae0-f24724392858" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Taylor Polynomial in Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a04d5e16-2468-543d-b47f-159fc11f1a9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194322} {:answer/id #uuid "160adcd1-500b-58a4-9ea5-d6e3eb59d6fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194323} {:answer/id #uuid "39166f28-5cf9-50de-b408-1f705693d257" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194324} {:answer/id #uuid "3f14f629-91ab-5120-9d35-8dae2bc0ba57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194325} {:answer/id #uuid "7b0d156a-6959-58c1-93a8-042b4d74867f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x + 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f14f629-91ab-5120-9d35-8dae2bc0ba57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194325} :answer-field/id #uuid "67819292-e7b9-5071-9ea9-6882b10c7f58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194321}] :question/id #uuid "2ec5ff3d-fd4d-5171-8304-f2a9e9fbb4f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-162989" :question/problem "For the function $f: R^{2} → R$, defined as\n\n$f(x, y) = e^{x + 2y}$,\n\nthe quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $a = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ is given by\n\n$f(x) \\approx ∗ + \\begin{bmatrix}1 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}∗ \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} + \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}∗ \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & ∗ \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}∗ \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nFind the sum of the six missing expressions."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198582 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e74c46c7-7f57-5adc-8acb-ea91958d8725" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Taylor Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffc96c81-5b7c-58cd-9b5d-6dfd9bb0b790" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194394} {:answer/id #uuid "3ee0489b-8a57-51af-bea6-34e805385b8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194395} {:answer/id #uuid "489f087f-0bcd-515e-9cfd-1985473f4899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194396} {:answer/id #uuid "5dc3c602-1423-5a20-94a7-1b05712f4b01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194397} {:answer/id #uuid "757dad5f-5217-5ec6-994f-193ccd359d89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ee0489b-8a57-51af-bea6-34e805385b8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194395} :answer-field/id #uuid "de5213ac-c95b-516a-8ebe-fbfb3ef5e679" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194393}] :question/id #uuid "6e6d1ba4-7501-5c84-a8cd-0bbe2d40c544" :question/math-academy-id "q-163113" :question/problem "For the function of two variables\n\n$f(x, y) = \\cos (x - 2y)$,\nthe quadratic Taylor polynomial of $f$ about $(0, 0)$ is given by\n$f(x, y) = 1 + ax^{2} + bxy + cy^{2}$.\nFind the value of $a + b + c$."}]}
